  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EA28-2016 Greek Refugee/Migrant and Economic Crisis</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This third Emergency Appeal from Caritas Hellas aims to improve the living conditions of refugees and migrants currently located in Greece. There are approximately 62,000 people in Greece who now need longer-term support. In addition, Caritas Hellas recognise that Greece has it&apos;s own on-going economic crisis, so this new EA will also aim to support the most vulnerable Greeks.
Specific objective 1 : Refugees, migrants and vulnerable Greek families meet their family basic needs 
Specific objective 2: Refugees and migrants at Diavata site (Thessaloniki Region)  live in container shelters 
Specific objective 3: Refugees and migrants are empowered  to integrate in Europe  

At the end of this appeal, there was an outstanding balance of &#x20ac; 110,180 which formed the incoming balance for EA22/2017 (GRC008) - which CAFOD has also supported.</narrative>
  </description>
